Maintainer: David Walther <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), bind9-dnsutils | dnsutils <!nocheck>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/moebiusV/wsl-dns-forward
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: wsl-dns-forward
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: make .local (mDNS) host names resolve inside WSL2
 A DNS forwarder for the loopback address.  Questions about .local names,
 which WSL2 cannot answer itself because it cannot see multicast traffic,
 are answered by a helper running in Windows PowerShell.  All other
 questions are passed to the normal upstream DNS server.
 .
 Aimed at Windows 10, where WSL has no DNS tunneling.  Installing the
 package does not change /etc/wsl.conf or /etc/resolv.conf; see
 /usr/share/doc/wsl-dns-forward/README.Debian for the setup steps.
